<title>ISRAEL: Israeli forex reserves rose to record in February.</title>
<headline>Israeli forex reserves rose to record in February.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's foreign currency reserves rose to a record $13.974 billion at the end of February, the Bank of Israel said on Sunday.</p>
<p>			  (in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>		  Feb 1997     Jan 1997	Feb 1996</p>
<p>Reserves	13,974	 12,792	   9,896</p>
<p>The central bank attributed the increase, which came to $2.51 billion in the first two months of the year, to capital imports by the Israeli private sector and continued overseas investment in Israel.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
</text>
